On Wed, Jan 28, 2015 at 2:26 AM, la durka <durka42@gmail.com> wrote:

> I think there has to be a distinction between "ordered set" and
> "sequence", no? Lojban seemingly conflates the two, but they're not the
> same -- a set, ordered or not, can't have duplicate elements, but a
> sequence can.
>

For me, porsi relates a sequence porsi1 to its members porsi3, so for me
there are no sets involved.

Since an ordered set is a special type of sequence, we could have
"rolcmipoi" or "cmipoi", "x1 porsi x2 lo ro cmima be x3" for ordered set, a
sequence whose members are the members of a set.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

